agent-ops task task-0cfbfe4f-e7ba-403c-95d5-995457eba0ac: agent-ops office: DOS-RPG office view of runs, worktrees and reviews
intent: Add explicit optional phase data to run state (planning/implementing/verifying/reviewing/integrating per run and worker, plus per-task latest verify/review result and passed/total criteria) written by the supervisor at deterministic transitions; a pure snapshot builder over every run in the git common dir, every agent-ops worktree and active review slots with per-worktree git diff --stat, changed paths and path-only narration (docs/** -> writing docs, tests/** -> writing tests, else editing <file>); a node:http GET-only loopback server with an unguessable URL token, Host check, 405 for non-GET, one server per repo recorded in <git common dir>/agent-ops/office.json, reuse when live, 10 idle minutes exit, launchd start on macOS and foreground elsewhere; `agent-ops office` prints/starts it and `run start`/`run status` print the URL; one inline HTML page (vanilla JS canvas, 16-color palette, character-matrix sprites, pixelated scaling, no asset files, ~2s polling) drawing a building with one floor per run (zones whiteboard/desk/lab bench/meeting table/front door, paper stack, bookshelf lit per passed criterion, wall clock budget, '!' for unanswered question, dialogue box), lobby desks for session worktrees, meeting room for review slots, and a click status window with copyable CLI commands; a pure scene-model function tested from snapshots. Never read native transcripts or file contents. Docs in README, docs/en/spec and docs/zh-TW/spec. No new dependencies.
criteria:
- phase-state: Run state records optional per-run and per-worker phase (planning, implementing, verifying, reviewing, integrating) set by the supervisor at each transition, plus per-task latest verify/review result and passed/total criteria; run state written before this change still validates and renders phase as unknown. Covered by unit tests in npm test.
- snapshot: A pure snapshot builder aggregates every run in the git common dir, every agent-ops worktree and active review/batch slots, with per-worktree diff stat, changed paths and decision-8 path-only narration (docs -> writing docs, tests -> writing tests, else editing <file>). Covered by unit tests on fixtures in npm test.
- server-cli: The office server (node:http) serves the page and snapshot JSON only with the token, only on 127.0.0.1 with a matching Host header, GET only (other methods 405), records itself in <git common dir>/agent-ops/office.json, is reused rather than duplicated, and exits after 10 idle minutes (tests with an injected clock); `agent-ops office` prints the URL starting the server if needed, and `run start` and `run status` print the office URL. Covered by server and CLI tests in npm test.
- scene: The page draws the DOS-RPG scene from in-code 16-color character-matrix sprites with no asset files, moves characters to their phase zone, and opens a status window with copyable commands on click; a pure scene-model function maps a snapshot to positions, paper count, lit books and '!' markers, covered by a unit test in npm test.
- docs-gates: README, docs/en/spec and the docs/zh-TW/spec mirror document `agent-ops office`; npm test, npm run package:check and the source scan pass.
